  "findings": [
    "All seven required workflows and all 20 jobs reached terminal state for the exact source SHA.",
    "Inventory, quality, loaded-plugin, desktop build, plugin-renderer, and all four Rust CI jobs passed: 17 jobs passed.",
    "All three Obsidian 1.14.4 round-trip jobs failed with the same source-hash error at reopen-asc. Invalid Direction.base changed from 122 bytes / SHA-256 fb9d112de60508c86bdde1c2ebf989143a379ff6ce59cc89e958865cfe43afe0 to 62 bytes / SHA-256 6db35053b1d4aa0aca718364f906cd8820193c635ba002958f953d1aa03548cc; the changed source retained the view type and name but dropped groupBy.",
    "All three reports show a settled first-open parse error for Omitted Direction.base and settled first-open SIDEWAYS capture. ASC was Alpha, Bravo, Zulu, None; DESC was Zulu, Bravo, Alpha, None, with matching row membership across OSes. The reopened app restored the SIDEWAYS view before the explicit ASC capture. Reopen observations for DESC, omitted, and SIDEWAYS were not completed after the strict hash failure.",
    "Inference from the artifacts: automatic restoration of the unsupported SIDEWAYS view on app startup triggered Obsidian's normalization and source rewrite. A focused repair should make a supported view active before shutdown, then explicitly select and capture SIDEWAYS after reopen while retaining strict source hashes.",
    "All workflows and job conclusions are exact-SHA; artifacts list their IDs, names, byte sizes, SHA-256 digests, and expiration timestamps. Executable validation ran only in GitHub Actions; no local executable validation was run."
  ]
